{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Circumcise the foreskin of your heart.</b> The deficiency of character traits and the formation from the aspect of their equivalence is called ערלה (foreskin), for every ערלה is an addition that is a deficiency; and whoever is ערל לב (uncircumcised of heart) has no power to receive intelligibles and to understand the way of truth." "<b>And do not stiffen your neck any more.</b> As you have stiffened until now, for he said to them (Exodus 33:3): ״כי עם קשה עורף אתה״ — for you are a stiff-necked people."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:14.950729461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}